      "summaries": {
        "en": "OpenRocket is a free, open-source software for simulating model rocket flights, helping enthusiasts and students design and test rockets safely before launch. It uses advanced physics engines to calculate aerodynamics, stability, and trajectory in real-time, incorporating factors like wind and motor performance. Users can build virtual rockets with drag-and-drop components, run simulations to optimize designs, and export data for analysis, making it ideal for educational projects or hobbyist experimentation.",
        "zh": "OpenRocket是一款开源模型火箭飞行模拟软件，通过精确的物理引擎计算空气动力学、稳定性和弹道轨迹，帮助用户在设计阶段预测火箭性能。它采用实时仿真技术，整合了风阻、发动机参数等变量，使模拟结果高度可靠。用户可通过拖拽组件构建虚拟火箭，运行模拟以优化设计，并导出数据进行分析，适用于教学演示或业余爱好者测试新创意，降低实际发射的风险与成本。",
        "es": "OpenRocket is a free, open-source software for simulating model rocket flights, helping enthusiasts and students design and test rockets safely before launch. It uses advanced physics engines to calculate aerodynamics, stability, and trajectory in real-time, incorporating factors like wind and motor performance. Users can build virtual rockets with drag-and-drop components, run simulations to optimize designs, and export data for analysis, making it ideal for educational projects or hobbyist experimentation.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "openrocket stands out for aerospace, flight-simulator, and java in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "OpenRocket is a free, open-source software for simulating model rocket flights, helping enthusiasts and students design and test rockets safely before launch. It uses advanced physics engines to calculate aerodynamics, stability, and trajectory in real-time, incorporating factors like wind and motor performance. Users can build virtual rockets with drag-and-drop components, run simulations to optimize designs, and export data for analysis, making it ideal for educational projects or hobbyist experimentation.",
